#WRITES
#AUTO 40
#NEEDED 0
# SARADC v1 conversion — read the analog gamepad inputs (sticks + button ladder).
#
# HISTORY (two wrong turns, both corrected on hardware).
#   1. The first version drove the v1 registers but read a constant 0x3FF on
#      every channel. That was misread as "the chip is a v2 part."
#   2. A v2 rewrite (registers at 0x104/0x110/0x120) was tried. The on-hardware
#      register DUMP (2026-07-02) DISPROVED it: the whole window mirrors a
#      16-byte block — DATA@0x00=0, STAS@0x04=0, CTRL@0x08=0, DLY_PU_SOC@0x0C=
#      0x08 (the documented v1 reset), repeating every 0x10. There are NO
#      distinct v2 registers; the chip decodes only 4 address bits here. So the
#      registers ARE v1 and present.
#   => The real bug was never the registers — it was the CONVERSION PROTOCOL.
#      The old probe skipped the mandatory power-DOWN-first step, wrote channel
#      select and power-up in a single write, and polled the wrong bit, so the
#      converter never ran cleanly and DATA held a saturated 0x3FF.
#
# This version follows the TRM Part1 §17.6 procedure exactly, per channel:
#   CTRL[3]=0  power DOWN the converter (clears its state)
#   CTRL[2:0]=ch + CTRL[5]=1   select channel, enable the EOC interrupt
#   CTRL[3]=1  power UP  — THIS starts the conversion (fires DLY_PU_SOC+2
#              sclk periods after power-up, then converts in ~13 clocks)
#   poll CTRL[6]  int_status = end-of-conversion, set to 1 when done
#   read DATA[9:0]  the 10-bit result
#
# Verified facts: CLKGATE_CON26@0xFDD20368 — clk_saradc bit8, pclk_saradc bit7
# (0=on). SOFTRST_CON24@0xFDD20460 — presetn_saradc bit0 (0=released; the old
# probe never released it). SARADC base 0xFE720000: DATA@0x00, STAS@0x04,
# CTRL@0x08 (bit6 EOC, bit5 int_en, bit3 power-up, bits2:0 channel 0..5).
#
# READING THE RESULT: a working read is a mid-scale value that MOVES with the
# input — hold a stick to one corner before/through the run and the channel(s)
# that are its axes read near 0x000 or 0x3FF while a centred axis reads ~0x200.
# A channel still stuck at a constant 0x3FF across positions means the analog
# front-end (reference/supply) needs bringing up — the next thing to chase.

LOG ===== SARADC v1 conversion (TRM 17.6) =====
LOG ungate SARADC clocks (CLKGATE_CON26 bits 7,8 -> 0)
W 0xFDD20368 0x01800000
LOG release SARADC reset (SOFTRST_CON24 presetn_saradc bit0 -> 0)
W 0xFDD20460 0x00010000
DELAY 20000
LOG confirm the four v1 registers (DATA, STAS, CTRL, DLY_PU_SOC)
DUMP 0xFE720000 4

LOG --- channel 0 ---
W 0xFE720008 0x00000000
DELAY 2000
W 0xFE720008 0x00000020
W 0xFE720008 0x00000028
DELAY 5000
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 20000
R 0xFE720000

LOG --- channel 1 ---
W 0xFE720008 0x00000000
DELAY 2000
W 0xFE720008 0x00000021
W 0xFE720008 0x00000029
DELAY 5000
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 20000
R 0xFE720000

LOG --- channel 2 ---
W 0xFE720008 0x00000000
DELAY 2000
W 0xFE720008 0x00000022
W 0xFE720008 0x0000002A
DELAY 5000
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 20000
R 0xFE720000

LOG --- channel 3 ---
W 0xFE720008 0x00000000
DELAY 2000
W 0xFE720008 0x00000023
W 0xFE720008 0x0000002B
DELAY 5000
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 20000
R 0xFE720000

LOG --- channel 4 ---
W 0xFE720008 0x00000000
DELAY 2000
W 0xFE720008 0x00000024
W 0xFE720008 0x0000002C
DELAY 5000
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 20000
R 0xFE720000

LOG --- channel 5 ---
W 0xFE720008 0x00000000
DELAY 2000
W 0xFE720008 0x00000025
W 0xFE720008 0x0000002D
DELAY 5000
POLL 0xFE720008 0x00000040 0x00000040 20000
R 0xFE720000

LOG SARADC v1 conversion complete — hold a stick to a corner and compare channels across positions
